 ### Whisper network/cache note
 
 The worker and inference run in the browser. The audio samples are not sent to a hosted speech-to-text API by this code path. On first use the browser must download the pinned Transformers.js runtime from `esm.sh` and the Whisper model files from Hugging Face; model caching is enabled where the browser permits it. Therefore this is **not a guaranteed first-run offline feature**. A cached model may be usable later offline only if the browser retained all required files and the app origin/runtime policy allows it. The `whisper-tiny` model can make recognition errors; manually review wording, names, punctuation, timestamps and speaker changes. No diarization or professional subtitle certification is claimed.
+
+## P50 production controls
+
+- **Cancel render:** Video Engine exposes `Hủy render` while a render is active. A single-export guard prevents concurrent recorder sessions. Cancellation stops the recorder/stream, cancels the animation frame, restores the playhead, rejects the render result and disables the cancel control after cleanup. The UI wrapper absorbs the expected cancellation rejection.
+- **Cancel Whisper:** `Hủy Whisper` invalidates the current job token, terminates the module worker if it exists, rejects and clears pending worker requests, and prevents a late decode/inference result from creating subtitle clips. During audio decoding, cancellation is cooperative: decoding itself may finish before the stale-job check returns.
+- **Release Whisper memory:** `Giải phóng model` terminates the worker and releases its in-memory pipeline/model references. Run this after transcription when the machine needs memory back. This does not erase files that the browser cache may have retained.
+- **Watchdog:** a worker request exceeding 15 minutes is terminated, pending work is rejected, and the UI receives actionable retry guidance.
+
+P50 exposes `cancelExport`, `whisperCancel` and `whisperUnload` on the existing Video Engine owner; no second timeline, persistence store or cloud service is introduced.
 
